      en: 'Mount Aso sits inside one of the largest calderas in the world, and Kusasenri is the most accessible part of it: a broad, grass-covered plain at the foot of Mount Eboshi, centred on two shallow ponds left by an ancient crater. Horses graze here for much of the year, and the Aso Volcano Museum stands at the edge of the grassland. Nakadake, the still-active crater a short drive further in, is currently closed to visitors, so this entry focuses on what is genuinely open: the grassland loop and the approach to Nakadake’s lower slopes.',
